//
// This implements the standard 1D Jacobi stencil:
//
//   B[i] = 1/3 * (A[i-1] + A[i] + A[i+1])
//   A[i] = 1/3 * (B[i-1] + B[i] + B[i+1])
//
// for interior points i in [1, n-2] and for tsteps time steps.
//
// Optimizations (while preserving exact semantics):
//   - Precompute the interior view once.
//   - Introduce a tunable spatial block size using into_blocks_dynamic +
//     hoist to iterate the interior domain in cache-friendly blocks,
//     without changing which points are updated or when.
//   - Reuse pre-built traversers for both sweeps inside the time loop.
//   - Keep the stencil weight in a local constant.
//
// All loop nests are expressed with Noarr traversers.
