	//   1. Restrict to the interior [1, n-2] via 'interior'.
	//   2. Split the interior i-range into blocks indexed by 'B' with
	//      (up to) i_block_size elements each (minor index keeps the name 'i').
	//   3. Hoist 'B' to the outermost level -> outer loop over blocks,
	//      inner loop over points inside each block.
